cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite the v2 result release.
  Protocol v1 is invalidated and its numbers may not be cited. Once the master
  paper — "After 2022: Japan's Search for a Novel Foreign Policy", of which this
  repository is the Chapter-4 evidence — is published, please cite that instead
  and this repository in addition.
title: "Backprop-NEAT — Summer"
abstract: >-
  A NumPy reconstruction of David Ha's Backprop-NEAT (2016), audited against
  hardmaru/backprop-neat-js and run as a frozen, preregistered two-track
  experiment: six conditions each removing one mechanism, ten paired replicates
  per task, and a sealed test evaluated exactly once. Experiment 2 of three in a
  research line on evolutionary search for open-world decision problems.
type: software
